  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive). No pair verb. Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{書|か}く.\n\nASPECT (ている):\nている marks the ongoing action: {書|か}いている = \"is writing.\" Note the te-form {書|か}いて (not {書|か}きて) — the regular pattern for godan verbs ending in く.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{手紙|てがみ}→手紙：00675_tegami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{書|か}く — to write a letter\n- ⟦{名前|なまえ}→名前：02234_namae⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{書|か}く — to write one's name\n- ⟦{日記|にっき}→日記：01486_nikki⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{書|か}く — to keep a diary\n- ⟦{書|か}き{方|かた}→書き方：13054_kakikata⟧ — how to write something\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{絵|え}→絵：02613_e⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{書|か}く is common in casual writing, but ⟦{絵|え}→絵：02613_e⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{描|か}く→描く：28436_kaku⟧ is the conventional spelling when a picture is meant. ⟦{描|えが}く→描く：02013_egaku⟧ is the same kanji read more formally, used of depicting scenes and feelings in art or writing. Keep {書|か}く for letters, characters, and text.\n- ⟦{記入|きにゅう}→記入：02624_kinyuu⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ is what official forms say where conversation would use {書|か}く.",
